        {
            "repo": "codefrak-oss/frakworks",
            "number": 28,
            "title": "Intake: Tier: 4 (opus low) — prescribed by the user; do not re-judge",
            "author": "lundmatt1-smith",
            "labels": [
                "intake"
            ],
            "url": "https://github.com/codefrak-oss/frakworks/issues/28",
            "createdAt": "2026-09-24T13:20:33Z",
            "updatedAt": "2026-09-24T13:21:45Z",
            "kind": "intake",
            "authorized": false,
            "flow": null,
            "pendingQuestion": {
                "id": 1,
                "intake": "b89b453e-b81a-11f1-8e2f-de53398f0b08",
                "repo": "codefrak-oss/frakworks",
                "issue": 28,
                "question": "The ask says to \"find and remove anything in the repo's MD files or claude.md files that reference the VMs or even Tailscale,\" reasoning that frakworks is starting fresh with a desktop Docker Compose stack and \"will not integrate with anything running on VMs.\" I looked for the README it names (\"What's here\" table + Deploy section assuming the collector VM) and found `observability/README.md` — but VM/Tailscale references aren't confined to that one stale doc. They're load-bearing across ~25 files, including ones describing infrastructure this repo's own CLAUDE.md still treats as live today: `bots/operator.md` (\"the fleet's runtime is the Linux VMs\"), `dispatch/README.md`, `bots/README.md` (the Oracle, \"a dedicated VM\"), `bots/webhook-wake/README.md` and `bots/secrets-mcp/README.md` (both front real endpoints with Tailscale Funnel/Serve), and `macrodata-refiner/server/README.md` / `macrodata-refiner/CLAUDE.md` (MDR itself is reached over Tailscale Funnel per this repo's own CLAUDE.md). `docs/framework-vs-deployment.md` also already treats tailnet names and VM numbers as *deployment values* to templatize, not concepts to delete — the repo's existing convention is placeholder-ize (`<collector-ip>`, `<tailnet>`), not erase.\n\nA blanket removal would delete accurate documentation of systems that are still running (the Oracle, MDR, webhook receiver, Smith-runner VMs) and contradicts the repo's own current CLAUDE.md description of the fleet. I don't want to guess which of these two the user meant and file a ticket that either guts working runbooks or misses the actual ask.\n\n```ask\nkind: choice\nquestion: How wide should the VM/Tailscale cleanup go?\noptions:\n  - id: narrow\n    label: Narrow — just observability/README.md's What's here/Deploy sections and the local-compose/framework-vs-deployment docs, to describe the desktop Compose path without erasing the (still-real) collector VM deploy notes\n  - id: broad\n    label: Broad — strip VM/Tailscale mentions everywhere, including bots/operator.md, webhook-wake, secrets-mcp and MDR docs, because those VMs are also going away, not just the observability collector\n  - id: other\n    label: Something else — I'll explain in a reply\nreply: label:answered\n```",
                "askedAt": "2026-09-24T13:21:44.625606Z",
                "answer": null,
                "answeredBy": null,
                "answeredAt": null
            }
        },
